{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1470340-custom-fancy-schmancy-character-sheet-thoughts","id":1470340,"title":"Custom, Fancy-Schmancy Character Sheet: Thoughts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-13T05:45:44-08:00","id":1470340,"title":"Custom, Fancy-Schmancy Character Sheet: Thoughts?","content":"I've created a super-fancy character sheet for my group, and I'd appreciate your feedback!<br /> <br /> Without further ado, here's the file! [<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KvkpnnMhumnXfCXBzOhR030HbnFQ-3Pi/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>]<br /> <br /> <br /> A couple caveats:<ul><li>Best viewed in &quot;two-page display&quot; mode, with the title page displayed on a seperate page. That would display it as intended, with (most of) the sheet viewed as two page spreads.</li> <li>My intent is to print this all off all fancy-like and put it in plastic sheet protectors, then giving everyone a wet/dry-erase marker. That should make it all super-readable, even with all the visual stuff.</li> <li>There's a couple visual glitches I'm still working out, forgive any minor issues.<ul><li>One of them (might be) the font on the &quot;ticket&quot; on the combat page. I'm not sure that saved correctly.</li> </ul></li> <li>This is an &quot;Origin&quot; level sheet. I've added space for the &quot;Hero&quot; level stuff, but I've blacked it out to keep things simple.</li> <li>This is very much specific to our campaign setting, which is a Camp Half-Blood rip-off based near Chicago--hence the graffiti, the setting-specific graphics, and so on.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Any thoughts on usability, or anything I might have left off? <br /> <br /> Also, I'm thinking about ripping out all the setting-specific stuff, creating an alternate printer-friendly version, and putting this up on drive-thru RPG. Is this something you'd pay $3-5 for? <br /> <br